R&C patch 7082: a PSO miss waits for its own cache slot; the FIFO lookahead decides every stop before reading a packet.

1. get_pso (rsx_live_draw.c) stores a missing pipeline's pending entry at slot n_psos, and since R&C patch 7050 then runs
the FIFO lookahead, whose nested get_pso calls append pending entries for the upcoming draws. The tail then awaited
slot n_psos - 1u. When the scan submitted at least one build, that slot is the LAST lookahead entry, so the draw that
missed was drawn with another draw's pipeline (other vertex/pixel shaders, input layout, possibly the GPU-fetch
variant) while its root parameters, vertex buffers and constants were its own, and the cache kept that pipeline
under the draw's key from then on. Nothing rejects it: both pipelines share the root signature, the scan only
covers draws on the same surface (same RTV/DSV formats), and root SRVs carry no bounds. The failing case is a miss whose
scan queues builds, e.g. FFA's first 3D frame (ffa-base-1: 9 new pipelines at 412.8-413.6 s, VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST
5 s later, the walker's fence wait never returns, RSX label 0x41 is never released, the main thread polls it in
func_006F5F38 for ever and the igPm job kernels sit in their normal LR idle wait at pc 0x3F750). A scan that queues
nothing leaves n_psos - 1u == the draw's slot, which is why the hang was intermittent (ToD with the lookahead on: 6/6
device lost, off: 0/2). ASSUMPTION: the exact GPU fault a mismatched pipeline causes is not identified; the mismatch
itself is the defect. Now get_pso keeps the slot it filled and the new header rsx_pso_slot.h
(rsx_pso_demand_tail) scans and then awaits that slot. Entries are only appended (a full cache returns before the
store) and the worker merge matches by key, so the index stays valid across the scan.
RPCS3 finds a draw's pipeline by that draw's own key (vertex program id, fragment program id, pipeline properties) and
fills the key's own entry when an asynchronous build finishes, never by a position in the cache [src:rpcs3-pso-cache].

2. rsx_fifo_ahead.h read a packet's arguments and handed them to the scan before checking the word budget, and checked
only the first method of an incrementing packet for the semaphore acquire 0x68. Now, before any argument is read: a
packet whose arguments reach put stops with RSX_AHEAD_PUT (the guest has not published those words yet), one over the
budget stops with RSX_AHEAD_LIMIT, and one whose methods include 0x68 on subchannel 0 stops with RSX_AHEAD_ACQUIRE.
After part 1 such guesses can no longer be bound to a draw, but they built pipelines from words the guest had not
written. The SPU reservation / LR-event code is not touched: it raises LR for every writer like RPCS3 does.

Default unchanged: the lookahead stays off (7050 0.3.1, LD_PSO_AHEAD=1 turns it on); with it off, and on a miss whose
scan queues nothing, behaviour is identical. Turning it back on by default is a separate step after a confirming run.
Host tests: R&C port/rc/tests/run_pso_demand_slot_test.sh (with a negative control: the pre-7082 tail must fail it)
and port/rc/tests/run_fifo_ahead_test.sh.

